{"version":"2.0","class":"dataset","label":"Population in regions, State cities and municipalities by age and gender at the beginning of the year by Territorial unit, Age, Sex and Time period","source":"Central Statistical Bureau of Latvia","updated":"2026-06-02T10:14:00Z","note":["<A HREF= https://stat.gov.lv/en/statistics-themes/environment/nature-resources/publications-and-infographics/21408-statistical TARGET=_blank>Additional information on statistical regions.</A>","<A HREF= https://stat.gov.lv/en/metadata/5911-population-and-key-demographic-indicators TARGET=_blank>Metadata</A>","... = Data not available or too uncertain for presentation","The State cities Jēkabpils, Ogre and Valmiera are also included in the figures for the corresponding municipalities.","Time series from 1971 to 2022: <A HREF= https://data.stat.gov.lv/pxweb/en/OSP_PUB/START/IRD040  TARGET=_blank> IRD040. Population in regions and cities by age and gender at the beginning of year </A>.","As of 2024, the territories of the statistical regions coincide with the territories of the planning regions.","In 2025, CSB changed the method for producing population estimates. Since 2012, a logistic regression model was used, but going forward, the SoL-logit model will be applied. The methods are similar, with the main difference being that the logistic regression model is a supervised model trained on data from the Population and Housing Census 2011, whereas the SoL-logit model is unsupervised model and does not require training data.\r\nTo ensure comparability, the data for 2023 and 2024 have also been recalculated using the new method.","The population estimate published on 2 June was revised on 2 October 2025, and the usually resident population now includes foreign students."],"role":{"time":["TIME"],"geo":["AREA"],"metric":["ContentsCode"]},"id":["ContentsCode","AREA","AGE","SEX","TIME"],"size":[1,57,1,1,15],"dimension":{"ContentsCode":{"label":"EliminatedContents","category":{"index":{"EliminatedV